# Real HIGH CVEs baked into AWS's current public.ecr.aws/lambda/python:3.12
# base image (verified 2026-08-06 against a fresh `docker pull`, image
# build amazon 2023.12.20260727) - not introduced by our code or Python
# dependencies (those are covered separately by pip-audit). Affects all 3
# Docker-based services identically, since they share this base image.
#
# None are reachable through anything our Lambda handlers actually do:
# gawk and rpm are OS utilities never invoked by our code (no shelling
# out, and Lambda's execution environment exposes no interactive shell to
# untrusted input anyway); glib2's xdgmime (MIME-type sniffing) is never
# called by our Python code either.
#
# Re-check by rebuilding + rescanning against a fresh base-image pull -
# AWS periodically ships patched builds under the same floating tag, which
# would silently resolve these without any change here. Re-check by:
# 2026-11-06 (3 months out).
CVE-2026-40467
CVE-2026-40468
CVE-2026-40553
CVE-2026-16118
CVE-2026-44605

# --- terraform/ config scan (added once terraform-security ran for real) ---

# S3 buckets and the SNS alerts topic use AWS-managed encryption (SSE-S3 /
# alias/aws/sns), not a customer-managed KMS key - a deliberate cost/
# complexity call already made and documented in docs/architecture.md's
# Observability section ("skipping ... a customer-managed KMS key as
# unnecessary for the current threat model/traffic"), not an oversight.
# AVD-AWS-0132 covers S3 (bootstrap's state bucket + both environments/prod
# buckets); AVD-AWS-0136 is the same call for the SNS topic.
AVD-AWS-0132
AVD-AWS-0136

# False positive, not a suppression of a real gap: aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block
# IS present for both environments/prod buckets (s3.tf, all 4 flags true -
# block_public_acls/block_public_policy/ignore_public_acls/restrict_public_buckets).
# Trivy's static analysis has a documented limitation linking a
# for_each-based public_access_block back to a for_each-based bucket with a
# computed name (aquasecurity/trivy#4997, #5001, #6385) - exactly this
# repo's shape (bucket name built from var.project_name + a random_id).
# Verified by reading s3.tf directly, not assumed.
AVD-AWS-0086
AVD-AWS-0087
AVD-AWS-0091
AVD-AWS-0093
